  "name": "DSO303 A2 - W1c auto-marking from AZ-B (AZ-A outage)",
  "category": "High Availability",
  "difficulty": "Advanced",
  "description": "Two-AZ serverless exam platform: Route 53 -> CloudFront + WAF -> API Gateway (Cognito JWT) -> Lambda in private subnets of both AZs -> DynamoDB autosave and Aurora PostgreSQL (writer AZ-A, reader AZ-B); presigned S3 uploads with lifecycle, SQS-driven marking and notifications, SES email.",
  "learningOutcome": "Exam peak absorbed by API Gateway, Lambda concurrency and on-demand DynamoDB; losing one AZ removes only that AZ's Lambda ENIs, NAT gateway and Aurora writer, which fails over to AZ-B.",
